I wake up to the loud sound of rain.
The rain is hitting my window hard.
I look outside at the grey sky of Mumbai.
Today is my birthday.
Today I have turned thirty-two.
This is my first birthday away from home.
I stand near the window and think.
I remember the month of January.
I came to Mumbai exactly six months ago.
At that time, the city was completely dry.
I came here just for a new job.
But now everything has changed.
The monsoon has completely transformed the streets.
There is only water everywhere.
It rained very heavily yesterday too.
And today the rain has not stopped either.
I like this weather very much.
I smile and get ready for my birthday.
